WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:12.450
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.470
<i>LINE.17  Start of the Mountains</i>

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.360
Being the captain sure is hard work.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.780
There was a pep rally suddenly 
scheduled for today, right?

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:38.780
<b>Sohoku High School
 Inter-High
 Soccer & Bicycle Racing Club
 Pep Rally</b>

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.780
Yeah.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.510
He's attending with Pierre-sensei.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:49.670
That's why the second-years have been 
asked to lead today's member meeting!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.290
We're meeting at Koga-san's place this year, right?

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.850
Come to think of it, Makishima-san's 
place was crazy last year.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.800
I wonder what Koga-san's house is like.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.860
It's a building, Naruko-kun!

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.340
Koga-san's house is a huge building!

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.810
A building?

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.530
That's an apartment building!

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.100
Onoda-kun, the entire building 
isn't Koga-san's house!

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.840
It's so tall!

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.270
That's just how apartment buildings are.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.210
There are so many cars!

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.690
Yeah, because a lot of people live here.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.800
Don't you have any relatives 
who live in apartments?

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.140
It's huge! It's so tall!

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.870
Another one who doesn't have any.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.010
Let's go.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.210
Ow, ow! Please stop, Aoyagi-san!

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.620
We're so high up!

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.740
This is crazy!

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.300
Hey, isn't that our school?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.680
Huh? What? Where?

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.090
Onoda-kun! Showoff!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.930
I'm losing my desire to stop them.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.430
<b>Kimitaka</b>

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.310
Sorry for making such a fuss.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.260
Sorry!

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.170
<i>I'll have to keep an eye 
on him during the race.</i>

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.310
Hey, thanks for coming.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.190
Let's get this meeting started.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.030
We won't be practicing riding,
 but stay focused.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.200
Yes, sir!

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.150
That's a huge monitor.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.790
Are we gonna watch a movie or something?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.370
It's data.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.020
Data?

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.530
Road racing is also a 
battle against the road.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.990
The upperclassmen used 
to say it all the time.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.980
This is data on this year's 
Tochigi Inter-High course.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:29.390
I attached a camera to my bike 
and rode the whole thing myself.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:30.130
What?

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.750
Whoa!

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.100
I told Aoyagi and Teshima what I was doing.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.360
<i>He rode the whole course alone?</i>

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.780
<i>Is this four-eyes serious?</i>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.860
<i>He said it so casually, but that's...</i>

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.740
<i>Koga-san is amazing!</i>

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:51.250
I felt things like small gaps and
 challenging sections not on the map.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:54.330
And now, I'll tell you all about them.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.040
Yes, sir!

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.090
That's all from me.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.550
To round things off,
 I have a question for you.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.550
Is there anything you want 
to try at the Inter-High?

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.990
If you're always on
 the defensive, you can't win.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.570
You'll never get any chances unless you try.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.360
Those are Junta's words.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.860
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.570
We'll go over them and incorporate anything 
that seems possible into our orders.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.860
You can speak freely.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.340
I want to cross the finish line!

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.360
Hey, hotshot! That's mine!

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.820
Saying it first doesn't mean you get it!

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.830
I'll be our ace and win the race!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.250
After all, I'm an all-rounder!

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.330
I'd like to go for the sprint.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.570
I'll be our ace!

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.730
Why not let me do it?

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.110
Your hair makes you stand out enough already.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.010
Well, yeah.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.390
But you stand out the 
most by finishing first!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.970
I'll do it! Seriously, I'll go anywhere!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:49.910
No, me!

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.090
Forget about you.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.270
No one's in agreement.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.930
I can do it!

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.050
Onoda.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:56.480
Huh?

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.220
Don't you have anything?

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.360
Oh, well...

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:06.160
I just want to ride as hard 
as I can and help the team.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.870
Oh, but...

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:15.540
If I can make just one request...

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.850
I made a promise over the winter.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.460
If possible...

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.720
I'd like to race against Hakone 
Academy's Manami Sangaku-kun.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.370
Somewhere.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.500
<i>Race...</i>

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.430
<i>I never thought I'd hear that word 
come from Onoda's mouth.</i>

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.420
Oh, actually...

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.460
When I ran into Manami-kun,

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:40.180
we talked about how nice the 
second day's mountains will be.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.070
But only if it's possible.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.950
What's important is the team's victory.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:48.950
I just...

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:56.370
I just want to give everything 
I have down to the very last drop.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:01.190
I want to experience that kind 
of race against Manami-kun again.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.450
That's all.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.720
You were last year's hero. 
What are you talking about?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.330
No one deserves to be selfish as much as you.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.540
Jeez, Onoda-kun.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.480
Yeah, you're being selfish.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.360
Let's do what we can to make that happen.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.420
Oh, no, no, no! Guys!

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:29.310
It doesn't have to happen! Really!

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.670
Don't be shy.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.580
I'll talk to Junta.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.540
I'm sure it'll depend on the situation, 
but I'll ask him to consider it.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:38.460
But...

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.710
<i>The second day's mountains, right?</i>

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.590
Next! Aoyagi, move up and pull!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.000
Yes, sir!

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.700
Keep up the pace! Focus!

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.880
We'll catch up to the front!

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:51.890
Yes, sir!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.390
I'll pull next!

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.610
Wait.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.250
Onoda, you don't need to 
be part of the rotation.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.600
Save your energy on these flats.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.270
Huh?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.920
That's an order, Onoda.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.440
Take the second day's mountain result!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.070
But, um, I...

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.950
It's starting to seem possible.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.200
We could reach the front.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.870
Be the motivation that makes us
 achieve that possibility, Onoda.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.500
<i>Motivation...</i>

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:27.060
You only need one goal 
when you're struggling.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.720
We'll take you to the mountains.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.310
That's right.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.800
I'll pull you there.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:35.890
<i>Imaizumi-kun.</i>

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.010
Onoda, don't speak and follow me!

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:41.890
<i>Imaizumi.</i>

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.150
Guys...

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.710
Thank you.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:52.200
Understood. I... I...

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.170
I'll conserve my energy with all my might!

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:57.460
Onoda-san.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.200
That's not something you 
do with all your might.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.440
Let's go, Sohoku!

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.450
Yeah!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.860
The lead pack is here!

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.590
Hakone Academy's in front!

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.010
Kyoto Fushimi's behind them!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.180
There's one Sohoku rider behind them!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.760
There are thirteen guys in the lead pack!

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.770
Fall back, Doubashi. Well done.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.770
Yuto, to the front.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.230
Your mountains are finally here.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.230
Yes, sir.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.020
They sent their climber to the front!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.400
Hakone Academy is in 
their mountain formation!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:37.310
<i>The course is entering a mountain 
stage with a wide, scenic road.</i>

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.660
<i>Beyond it rises the treasure of Gunma,</i>

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.000
<i>which houses the Ikaho Hot Spring
 along its slope.</i>

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:47.040
<i>Rising 1,391 meters above sea level is</i>

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.180
<i>Mount Haruna.</i>

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:57.040
<i>The second day's mountain line is at 
the highest point of National Route 33,</i>

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.890
<i>which runs along the mountainside,
 at 1,170 meters.</i>

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.190
Why do you keep glancing behind you, Manami?

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.610
Focus on the race.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:17.280
I was just thinking about how nice the 
weather is and wanted to check out the view.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.210
Just kidding.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.960
I can't fool you, can I?

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.790
No.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.990
You're not worried about
 Kyoto Fushimi behind us, are you?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.580
Is it someone behind them?

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.290
Yes.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:36.000
We're riding hard at the Inter-High,
 but you're thinking about your own race?

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.260
I suppose I am.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:42.260
Wouldn't it be a waste not to race here?

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:47.600
The team's doing well, and I took the
 first day's mountains like I was ordered to.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.440
Is it Sohoku's four-eyes?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.620
Yes, him.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.570
We made a promise.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:56.490
You can't.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.660
I've been asked to lead the 
team through the mountains.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.630
We have over ten kilometers
 of climb ahead of us.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:05.990
You should rest.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.750
If we send anyone, it'll be Yuto.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.290
The Inter-High has a third day.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.210
If we send our ace climber today

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:18.130
and you're too tired to ride tomorrow, 
then our strategy will be ruined.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.570
Huh?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:22.740
Kuroda-san.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:27.980
Riding hard today so I can take it easy tomorrow

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.150
is not how I'm approaching this race.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:37.650
<i>His focus is increasing as we 
get closer to the mountains.</i>

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:42.140
Sorry. When he shows up, I'm going.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.510
<i>What kind of reason is that, Manami?</i>

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.290
<i>He overrode Kuroda-san's orders.</i>

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:51.810
<i>There's no argument that will convince him.</i>

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:56.180
<i>Riding without reason
 is his greatest strength.</i>

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.360
I understand what you want.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.130
But...

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.720
But, Manami, there are two conditions 
that will prevent you from going.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:09.090
The first is if Sohoku doesn't make it here.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.650
If the four-eyes in question never shows up.

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:17.030
<i>I don't know why he even thinks 
Sohoku will catch up.</i>

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:20.150
<i>But he's an oddball.</i>

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.070
What's the second one?

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.070
Second...

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.580
We're entering the final 
mountains of the second day.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.660
Kyoto Fushimi and Midousuji 
haven't won any titles yet.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.030
He'll make his move before long.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.290
You won't have time to race.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.170
Kuroda-san! Kyoto Fushimi's on the move!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:41.970
There's three of them!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:46.470
Second-year climber Kiriya and 
third-year launching pad Mizuta

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.890
are accompanying their ace, Midousuji!

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.330
Yuto, Manami!

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:54.860
Stop them!

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:01.960
You're not going anywhere.

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.470
You heard him.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:10.810
<i>You're right. If they get ahead,
 then I won't get to race, Kuroda-san.</i>

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.580
They're so fast!

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
They stopped us immediately.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.170
These are Hakone Academy's climbers?

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.510
One more time.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.700
We'll attack again!

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:25.170
What?

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.070
Huh?

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.510
Wait. Wait, Midousuji-kun.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:29.890
We're still out of breath.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.700
We can't do that again right away.

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.390
We will.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:39.090
Kiriya-kun, are you stronger 
than the two in front of us?

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.030
Wh-What?

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.860
Of course not.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.570
They're good enough to be aces in 
terms of both strength and power.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:49.910
Right? Then there's only 
one thing you can do.

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:55.120
If you're inferior in every way,
 then all you can do

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.450
is pedal like your life depends on it.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:02.380
And now is the time.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.490
Resume Phase 28!

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.800
Keep pedaling until your legs break!

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.180
Kyoto Fushimi is accelerating!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.970
They're attacking again!

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:17.400
Our attack must succeed, Zakus!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.110
Manami, Yuto! After them!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:21.960
Got it.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.680
I know.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:26.400
I'll stop this attack.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.410
After all, I have my own plans.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.100
Go!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.370
They caught up in a flash!

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.960
And he passed us!

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.460
<i>The wind?</i>

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.850
<i>I thought I saw wings for a second.</i>

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.560
Sorry, but you're not going 
anywhere, Midousuji-kun.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.270
<i>They're monsters. They're on 
a different level from us.</i>

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.850
<i>We can't fight against them and win!</i>

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.610
Manami.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.410
It's been a while.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.510
I don't think we've spoken 
since last year's Inter-High.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:12.110
<i>A guy who enjoys fighting.</i>

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.240
<i>A guy whose talents are wasted.</i>

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.510
<i>A guy who isn't a Zaku.</i>

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:24.840
The guy who lost to Sakamichi last year!

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:29.260
Brutal! He's hitting him where it hurts.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.350
If I were in his position, that's the
 last thing I'd want to hear.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.890
Oh, that?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:39.770
Huh?

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:44.070
If losing bothers me,
 I should remove my jersey.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.280
That's what he told me.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.280
But I'm still wearing mine.

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:54.330
I realized then

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.020
that I was still in the middle.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.180
It's not over yet.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.670
I'm glad I didn't end it.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:07.170
Someone even faster than me 
is waiting beyond the peak.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.080
What could be more exciting?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.430
I can go all out at the peak.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:19.810
It means I'll feel even more 
alive than I ever have before.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.400
<i>This man, Manami...</i>

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:32.280
<i>I thought he'd given up after being 
hurt last year, but now I know.</i>

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:35.830
<i>He's in perfect condition.</i>

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.500
<i>This attack won't go well.</i>

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:43.380
Resume Phase 28, Zakus!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.300
I-I can't! Midousuji-kun, let's fall back!

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:48.700
This is reckless!

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:49.900
Hey, Kiriya!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.260
This attack can't possible succeed—

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:58.470
I said we're doing it now.

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:05.670
I have my reasons, but you don't need 
to know what they are right now.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:09.550
We have to make it happen now.

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:18.450
<i>Cheers from behind? Could it be?</i>

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:24.620
<i>They're coming now?</i>

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:27.570
Hey, you hear that?

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.080
Yeah, Kuroda-san.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:31.210
There's noise coming from 
behind us, Yamaguchi-san!

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.430
Is someone coming?

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.090
A Sohoku rider?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.560
There's a lot of them. It's not just one rider.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.390
That's...

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.370
I see the front!

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.900
Higo blooms again!

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:48.770
<i>It's not Sohoku.</i>

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.230
K-Kumamoto Daiichi.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.810
That's right!

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:55.350
We're the Higo Superexpress, 
Kumamoto Daiichi!

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.430
Did they pass them?

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.240
It's not Sohoku?

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:07.930
My Zakus reported that they 
were plotting to catch up later

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:10.960
while they were in the pack.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.840
But they actually did it.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.380
What perfect timing.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:20.260
I'll use everything I can.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.560
Now's my chance.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.140
We'll use this confusion to our advantage.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:32.040
I'm the rumored Kumamoto Daiichi captain,
 the Demon Sergeant Ise Shinya!

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.270
Surprised? This is Kumamoto Daiichi!

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.850
No one's team is stronger than ours!

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.530
Our team makes the impossible possible!

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.170
Kumamoto is amazing!

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.950
They caught up in the mountains!

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:47.080
<i>Seriously, Kumamoto Daiichi?</i>

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.210
<i>They passed Sohoku?</i>

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:53.430
Fujiwara, once we catch up to them, 
wait for an opportunity to jump ahead.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.630
I expect you to win the 
mountain result number tag.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.870
You can count on me, Ise-san.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:01.550
I promise I won't let Kumamoto Daiichi down!

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:05.730
<i>Did Kyoto Fushimi get ahead 
while we were distracted?</i>

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:09.150
<i>No, they didn't.</i>

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:16.430
<i>What's important during road 
races is to predict the future</i>

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:20.370
<i>during any confusion and calmly 
deceive the eyes of others.</i>

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:24.850
<i>Kuroda-kun is keeping an eye on me.</i>

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:28.000
<i>First, I have to make him lower his guard.</i>

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:30.150
We're skipping ahead to Phase 108.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.450
Pretend you're exhausted.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.020
Got it.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:32.630
Yes, sir.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:37.050
Tell the other Zakus, Mizuta-kun.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.940
Stay toward the right side of the course,

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:45.350
and let Kumamoto Daiichi come 
between us and Hakone Academy.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:48.970
What? Are you sure we 
should let them join us?

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:53.190
Their captain just said Kumamoto Daiichi's 
team is stronger than anyone else's!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:57.190
What? Team strength?

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.700
That's just what they say about themselves.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:10.170
We finally caught up to the front.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.500
<i>I was wrong.</i>

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:18.760
<i>I thought it was you, Sakamichi-kun.</i>

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:26.690
<i>And since no one's left yet,
 I thought we could go together.</i>

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:32.410
<i>He's replenishing his fluids.</i>

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:34.420
<i>It doesn't look like they'll 
attack anytime soon.</i>

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.030
Hey, Manami! How long are you 
going to keep looking behind you?

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.700
Now, Zakus!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:51.700
Without making a single sound, hold your
 breath and silently go all out!

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.260
Kyoto Fushimi?

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:03.470
Yuki!

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:14.480
Can you do it, Junta?

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.270
Probably. It's pretty likely.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:19.400
Really?

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.550
Everyone's motivated.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:26.240
In the next few minutes,
 we should see the lead pack.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:28.500
Look, it's Sohoku!

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.250
Last year's champions 
are racing up the slope!

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.210
They fell apart once, but they're
 back together again!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.130
They'll catch up to the front!

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.130
Onoda!

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.300
Yes, sir!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.030
Were you able to conserve your energy?

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.790
Yes, sir!

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:44.680
I have orders for you!

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.730
Once we join the lead pack, jump ahead!

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:52.610
Push Hakone Academy's Manami aside and 
cross the second day's mountain line first!

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.520
Yes, sir!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.650
I see them!

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.530
<i>Damn.</i>

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.940
<i>We caught up.</i>

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.390
<i>Hakone Academy, Kyoto Fushimi, and Naruko.</i>

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:07.490
<i>We're here.</i>

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:10.160
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:16.670
<i>What is this? Kumamoto Daiichi?</i>

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:23.860
Teshima-san, the Kumamoto Daiichi 
team that passed us is scattered.

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:26.360
Yeah. Don't drop your pace.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:27.780
Let's keep going.

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.680
Yes, sir.

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:32.810
<i>What's going on? What in the world happened?</i>

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:09.310
I'm hungry.

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:11.480
Let's get something on the way home.

00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:12.320
I want pizza.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.770
There it is! Your suggestion for pizza!

00:23:14.770 --> 00:23:17.660
Let's get something else 
once in a while, like curry.

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:18.880
We're getting pizza today.

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:20.300
I decided we would this morning.

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:22.580
You said the same thing when 
we got pizza last time.

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:23.500
Pizza!

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.650
No, we're getting curry today!

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:27.630
Aoyagi, say something.

00:23:28.310 --> 00:23:29.410
In that case...

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.090
<b>Made in our proud brick oven</b>

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.090
<b><i>Famous curry pizza restaurant!!</i></b>

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.090
There's this famous curry pizza restaurant!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:37.010
<b><i>Famous curry pizza
 restaurant!!</i></b>

00:23:36.990 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT LINE  Naruko's Determination</i>

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:39.890
<b><i>Famous curry pizza
 restaurant!!</i></b>

